- id: TF-01FE4A3F88
  title: Secret material committed to the repository
  category: Information Disclosure
  element: k8s:Secret:shop/shop-db
  severity: critical
  description: Secret shop/shop-db contains inline `data`/`stringData` in a manifest tracked in version
    control. base64 is an encoding, not encryption. Anyone with repository read access -- including every
    CI job, every fork, and the full git history after the value is "removed" -- has these credentials.
    Rotation is the only remedy once this has been pushed.
  evidence:
  - description: 'inline keys: password, username'
    observed:
    - password
    - username
    location: k8s/app.yaml:80
  risk:
    score: 20
    likelihood: 4
    impact: 5
    exposure_hops: 4
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-798
    - CWE-540
    - CWE-312
    mitre:
    - T1552.001
    - T1552.008
    cis:
    - 5.4.1
    nist:
    - IA-5
    - SC-28
    owasp:
    - K08
  rule_id: TF-DATA-001
  mitigation:
