    mitre:
    - T1610
    cis:
    - 5.2.6
    nist:
    - AC-6
    owasp:
    - K01
  rule_id: TF-K8S-003
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Run as a dedicated non-root UID.
    effort: medium
- id: TF-145F8091F6
  title: Internet-reachable workload has no ingress NetworkPolicy
  category: Spoofing
  element: k8s:Deployment:shop/storefront
  severity: critical
  description: Deployment shop/storefront is reachable from the internet and no NetworkPolicy restricts
    ingress to it. Kubernetes networking is flat by default, so once an attacker has code execution in
    any pod in the cluster they can reach this workload directly on its pod IP -- and this workload can
    reach everything else. Segmentation is the control that turns one compromised pod into one compromised
    pod rather than a cluster-wide incident.
  evidence:
  - description: no NetworkPolicy selects this workload for ingress
    observed: false
    location: k8s/app.yaml:7
  - description: hops from internet = 2
    observed: 2
    location: k8s/app.yaml:7
  risk:
    score: 20
    likelihood: 4
    impact: 5
    exposure_hops: 2
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-923
    - CWE-1327
    mitre:
    - T1210
    - T1046
    cis:
    - 5.3.2
    nist:
    - SC-7
    - AC-4
    owasp:
    - K05
  rule_id: TF-NET-001
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Apply default-deny ingress in the namespace, then allow only required sources.
    effort: medium
