- id: TF-3213D7BD6D
  title: Pod shares the host network namespace
  category: Spoofing
  element: k8s:Deployment:shop/storefront
  severity: high
  description: 'Deployment shop/storefront runs with hostNetwork: true. The pod shares the node''s network
    namespace, so it can sniff traffic destined for other pods on the node, bind to privileged node ports,
    bypass NetworkPolicy entirely (policies do not apply to host-network pods), and reach the kubelet
    on localhost:10250.'
  evidence:
  - description: spec.hostNetwork is true
    observed: true
    location: k8s/app.yaml:7
  risk:
    score: 16
    likelihood: 4
    impact: 4
    exposure_hops: 2
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-668
    mitre:
    - T1040
    - T1610
    cis:
    - 5.2.4
    nist:
    - SC-7
  rule_id: TF-K8S-006
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Use the pod network and expose the workload through a Service.
    effort: medium
- id: TF-5C511CED45
  title: Pod shares the host PID or IPC namespace
  category: Information Disclosure
  element: k8s:Deployment:shop/storefront
  severity: high
  description: Sharing hostPID lets the container see and signal every process on the node, and read secrets
    from other processes' /proc/<pid>/environ. Sharing hostIPC exposes shared memory segments belonging
    to other workloads.
  evidence:
  - description: spec.hostPID
    observed: true
    location: k8s/app.yaml:7
  - description: spec.hostIPC
    observed: false
    location: k8s/app.yaml:7
  risk:
    score: 16
    likelihood: 4
    impact: 4
    exposure_hops: 2
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-668
    mitre:
    - T1057
    - T1611
    cis:
    - 5.2.2
    - 5.2.3
    nist:
    - SC-4
  rule_id: TF-K8S-007
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Remove hostPID and hostIPC.
    effort: low
- id: TF-0147A11831
  title: Container adds dangerous Linux capabilities
  category: Elevation of Privilege
  element: k8s:Container:shop/storefront/sidecar-agent
  severity: high
  description: Container shop/sidecar-agent adds capabilities SYS_ADMIN, NET_RAW. SYS_ADMIN is close to
    full root; SYS_PTRACE allows reading memory of other processes; NET_ADMIN permits traffic redirection
    and ARP spoofing; SYS_MODULE allows loading kernel modules, which is a direct host takeover.
  evidence:
  - description: capabilities.add = SYS_ADMIN, NET_RAW
    observed:
    - SYS_ADMIN
    - NET_RAW
    location: k8s/app.yaml:41
  risk:
    score: 16
    likelihood: 4
    impact: 4
    exposure_hops: 3
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-250
    mitre:
    - T1611
    cis:
    - 5.2.8
    - 5.2.9
    nist:
    - AC-6
    - CM-7
  rule_id: TF-K8S-008
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Drop ALL, then add back only the minimum.
    effort: low
- id: TF-00CDA7D7B5
  title: NodePort service exposes the workload on every node
  category: Spoofing
  element: k8s:Service:shop/postgres
  severity: high
  description: A NodePort opens the port on every node in the cluster. Whether that is internet-reachable
    depends entirely on node security groups, which are usually managed by a different team than the manifest
    -- so this is exposure you cannot verify from the manifest alone.
  evidence:
  - description: nodePorts = 30432
    observed:
    - 30432
    location: k8s/app.yaml:129
  risk:
    score: 16
    likelihood: 4
    impact: 4
    exposure_hops: 1
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-668
    mitre:
    - T1133
    nist:
    - SC-7
  rule_id: TF-NET-009
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Prefer ClusterIP behind an Ingress; if NodePort is required, restrict node security groups.
    effort: medium
- id: TF-AF714E2121
  title: Object storage bucket has a public ACL
  category: Information Disclosure
  element: tf:aws_s3_bucket.assets
  severity: high
  description: 'aws_s3_bucket assets is configured with a public-read or public-read-write ACL. Public
    buckets are found by automated scanners within hours. public-read-write is worse than disclosure:
    anyone can also overwrite objects, which turns the bucket into a malware distribution point under
    your domain.'
  evidence:
  - description: resource aws_s3_bucket with public ACL
    observed: aws_s3_bucket
    location: tf/main.tf:1
  risk:
    score: 15
    likelihood: 3
    impact: 5
    exposure_hops: null
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-732
    - CWE-284
    mitre:
    - T1530
    nist:
    - AC-3
    - SC-28
  rule_id: TF-CLOUD-001
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Set the ACL to private and enable the account-level public access block.
    effort: low
- id: TF-130F0EFF4C
  title: Database instance is publicly accessible
  category: Information Disclosure
  element: tf:aws_db_instance.shop
  severity: high
