    - CWE-798
    mitre:
    - T1552.001
    nist:
    - IA-5
    - SC-28
  rule_id: TF-CLOUD-007
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Rotate the credential, move it to a secret manager, and encrypt remote state.
    effort: medium
- id: TF-908B3685D9
  title: Hardcoded credential in Terraform source
  category: Information Disclosure
  element: tf:aws_instance.worker
  severity: high
  description: aws_instance worker has a credential-shaped attribute with a literal value. Terraform source
    is version-controlled, and any value here is also written in cleartext into the state file, which
    is frequently stored in a bucket with broader read access than the repository.
  evidence:
  - description: literal credential attribute detected
    observed: aws_instance
    location: tf/main.tf:24
  risk:
    score: 15
    likelihood: 3
    impact: 5
    exposure_hops: null
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-798
    mitre:
    - T1552.001
    nist:
    - IA-5
    - SC-28
  rule_id: TF-CLOUD-007
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Rotate the credential, move it to a secret manager, and encrypt remote state.
    effort: medium
- id: TF-B49848DD9B
  title: Secret is reachable from an internet-facing workload
  category: Information Disclosure
  element: k8s:Secret:shop/shop-db
  severity: high
  description: Secret shop/shop-db is only 4 hops from the internet along the data-flow graph. An RCE
    in the internet-facing component in that chain yields this secret directly. This is not a misconfiguration
    on its own -- it is a statement about blast radius that should drive where you invest in detection.
  evidence:
  - description: shortest path from internet = 4 hops
    observed: 4
    location: k8s/app.yaml:80
  risk:
    score: 15
    likelihood: 3
    impact: 5
    exposure_hops: 4
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-522
    mitre:
    - T1552
    nist:
    - SC-28
    - AC-6
  rule_id: TF-DATA-003
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Shorten the trust chain -- scope the secret, or broker access through a short-lived token.
    effort: high
- id: TF-DB2F8BA20D
  title: Secret material in build instructions
  category: Information Disclosure
  element: docker:image:Dockerfile#node:latest
  severity: high
  description: 'DockerImage node:latest embeds credential-shaped values in ENV/ARG/RUN. Docker layers
    are immutable and independently pullable: deleting the value in a later layer does not remove it,
    and anyone who can pull the image can extract it with `docker history` or by unpacking the layer tarballs.'
  evidence:
  - description: credential-like build instructions detected
    observed:
    - value: ARG NPM_TOKEN=***
      line: 2
    - value: ENV DB_PASSWORD=***
      line: 5
    location: Dockerfile:2
  risk:
    score: 15
    likelihood: 3
    impact: 5
    exposure_hops: null
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-798
    - CWE-540
    mitre:
    - T1552.001
    cis:
    - '4.10'
    nist:
    - IA-5
  rule_id: TF-DKR-003
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Rotate the credential and use BuildKit secret mounts.
    effort: medium
- id: TF-E068498B05
  title: Container does not drop all capabilities
  category: Elevation of Privilege
  element: k8s:Container:shop/postgres/postgres
  severity: high
  description: Container shop/postgres keeps the default Docker capability set (CHOWN, DAC_OVERRIDE, FOWNER,
    SETUID, SETGID, NET_RAW and others). SETUID/SETGID enable local privilege escalation via setuid binaries;
    NET_RAW enables ARP/DNS spoofing against pods sharing the node network.
  evidence:
  - description: capabilities.drop does not include ALL
    observed: []
    location: k8s/app.yaml:115
  risk:
    score: 12
    likelihood: 3
    impact: 4
    exposure_hops: 3
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-250
    mitre:
    - T1548
    cis:
    - 5.2.9
    nist:
    - CM-7
  rule_id: TF-K8S-009
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Drop ALL capabilities as the baseline.
    effort: low
- id: TF-22E505D1B7
  title: Container root filesystem is writable
  category: Tampering
  element: k8s:Container:shop/postgres/postgres
  severity: high
  description: 'A writable root filesystem lets an attacker with code execution drop a web shell, overwrite
    application binaries, or install persistence that survives a process restart. It also removes a cheap
    tripwire: with a read-only root, most post-exploitation tooling fails immediately and noisily.'
  evidence:
  - description: readOnlyRootFilesystem is not true
    observed: false
    location: k8s/app.yaml:115
  risk:
    score: 12
    likelihood: 3
    impact: 4
    exposure_hops: 3
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-732
    mitre:
    - T1505.003
    - T1543
    cis:
    - 5.2.11
    nist:
    - SI-7
  rule_id: TF-K8S-010
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Make the root filesystem read-only and mount emptyDir for writable paths.
    effort: medium
- id: TF-C38E0336C5
  title: Container has no CPU or memory limits
  category: Denial of Service
  element: k8s:Container:shop/postgres/postgres
  severity: high
  description: 'Without resource limits, Container shop/postgres can consume all allocatable CPU and memory
    on its node. A memory leak or a deliberately expensive request becomes a node-wide outage: the kubelet
    begins evicting neighbouring pods, and a single compromised workload becomes a cluster-wide denial
    of service primitive.'
  evidence:
  - description: resources.limits.cpu is unset
    observed: true
    location: k8s/app.yaml:115
  - description: resources.limits.memory is unset
    observed: true
    location: k8s/app.yaml:115
  risk:
    score: 12
    likelihood: 3
    impact: 4
    exposure_hops: 3
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-770
    - CWE-400
    mitre:
    - T1499
    cis:
    - 5.7.3
    nist:
    - SC-5
    owasp:
    - K07
  rule_id: TF-K8S-013
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Set requests and limits; enforce defaults with a LimitRange.
    effort: low
- id: TF-325D409A9E
  title: Pod does not set a seccomp profile
  category: Elevation of Privilege
  element: k8s:StatefulSet:shop/postgres
  severity: high
  description: No seccomp profile is applied, so the container may issue all ~350 syscalls. Most container
    escapes published in the last several years relied on syscalls that RuntimeDefault blocks outright.
  evidence:
