- id: TF-5AF47A662A
  title: Database deletion protection and final snapshot are both disabled
  category: Denial of Service
  element: tf:aws_db_instance.shop
  severity: low
  description: aws_db_instance shop can be destroyed with no snapshot retained. A compromised CI credential,
    or a plain mistake in a `terraform apply`, results in unrecoverable data loss -- this is the destructive
    end of the availability spectrum.
  evidence:
  - description: skip_final_snapshot = true and deletion_protection = false
    observed: true
    location: tf/main.tf:5
  risk:
    score: 3
    likelihood: 1
    impact: 3
    exposure_hops: null
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-1188
    mitre:
    - T1485
    nist:
    - CP-9
    - CP-10
  rule_id: TF-CLOUD-010
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Enable deletion protection and keep final snapshots.
    effort: low
- id: TF-7A6B484985
  title: Image has no HEALTHCHECK
  category: Denial of Service
  element: docker:image:Dockerfile#node:latest
  severity: low
  description: Without a HEALTHCHECK, a container that has hung but not exited is indistinguishable from
    a healthy one outside Kubernetes (where probes cover this).
  evidence:
  - description: no HEALTHCHECK instruction
    observed: false
    location: Dockerfile:1
  risk:
    score: 3
    likelihood: 1
    impact: 3
    exposure_hops: null
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-703
    cis:
    - '4.6'
    nist:
    - SI-4
  rule_id: TF-DKR-006
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Add a HEALTHCHECK.
    effort: low
- id: TF-12B0D70662
  title: Service account token automounted but unused API access
  category: Elevation of Privilege
  element: k8s:StatefulSet:shop/postgres
  severity: low
  description: automountServiceAccountToken is unset, so a projected API token is mounted at /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount.
    If the workload does not call the Kubernetes API, this token is pure attack surface -- it is the first
    thing post-exploitation tooling looks for.
  evidence:
  - description: automountServiceAccountToken is unset (defaults to true)
    observed: null
    location: k8s/app.yaml:99
  risk:
    score: 3
    likelihood: 1
    impact: 3
    exposure_hops: 2
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-522
    mitre:
    - T1528
    cis:
    - 5.1.6
    nist:
    - AC-6
  rule_id: TF-K8S-017
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Set automountServiceAccountToken false unless the pod calls the API server.
    effort: low
- id: TF-5E484B5FBE
  title: Namespace has no Pod Security Admission enforcement
  category: Elevation of Privilege
  element: k8s:Namespace:default/shop
  severity: low
  description: Namespace shop sets no pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce label. Nothing prevents someone
    deploying a privileged, host-mounting pod here tomorrow, which means every workload-level fix in this
    report can be silently undone.
  evidence:
  - description: no enforce label
    observed: null
    location: k8s/app.yaml:2
  risk:
    score: 3
    likelihood: 1
    impact: 3
    exposure_hops: null
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-693
    mitre:
    - T1610
    cis:
    - 5.2.1
    nist:
    - CM-7
    - AC-6
    owasp:
    - K01
  rule_id: TF-NET-012
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Label the namespace with a Pod Security Standard.
    effort: low
- id: TF-2DF6ADA177
  title: Data store encryption status cannot be determined
  category: Information Disclosure
  element: tf:aws_s3_bucket.assets
  severity: low
  description: No encryption attribute is set on aws_s3_bucket assets. Some providers default to encrypted
    and some do not, and raw HCL parsing cannot resolve module defaults -- so this needs a human check
    rather than an assumption.
  evidence:
  - description: no encryption attribute present
    observed: aws_s3_bucket
    location: tf/main.tf:1
  risk:
    score: 2
    likelihood: 1
    impact: 2
    exposure_hops: null
  references:
    cwe:
    - CWE-311
    nist:
    - SC-28
    - CM-6
  rule_id: TF-CLOUD-005
  mitigation:
    status: open
    description: Set the encryption attribute explicitly so the intent is reviewable.
    effort: low
- id: TF-42921CADEB
  title: Compose service has no resource limits
  category: Denial of Service
  element: compose:service:cache
  severity: low
  description: No CPU or memory limit is set, so this container can exhaust the host.
  evidence:
  - description: deploy.resources.limits is unset
    observed: true
